This project adapts ideas and some wording from the following MIT-licensed works:

obra/superpowers (https://github.com/obra/superpowers), Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent, MIT License.
  Adapted: the brainstorming interview style (one question at a time, play back understanding,
  plain-language defaults), the writing-plans header and task format, "never pass session history
  to subagents", "rulings, not stalls", the progress ledger, the stop list for destructive or external
  actions, the implementer status contract, verification-before-completion (no claim without fresh
  evidence), failing-test-first from test-driven-development, root cause before fix from
  systematic-debugging, and Critical/Important/Minor review triage from requesting-code-review.

olsenbrands/fable-foreman (https://github.com/olsenbrands/fable-foreman), MIT License.
  Adapted: the blind verifier that sees only the task and acceptance criteria, assumes the work is
  broken and must reproduce evidence, and the fixed worker report contract.
